   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Base: music, dialogue or action\n\nOne shot per image over your track, in order. Load a track and your images, pick **mode** and press Run.\n\n- **mode**: *music* cuts whole bars from the downbeat after *start_at*, guided by the kick of **drums**; *dialogue* cuts in the pauses, guided by **voice**; *action* cuts between hits, guided by the track.\n- **Audio Separation** feeds **drums** and **voice** from your track, so switching mode is one click.\n- **duration**: how long the video runs from *start_at*. One image and 30 s gives one 30 s shot.\n- **Context windows**: each shot is sampled in overlapping ~5 s windows, so shots can run 30 s and more and keep their look. Bypass the node for the tightest sync on short shots.\n- **Anchor**: every shot also sees this image as <Picture 2>, which holds the people and style across the cuts. Default: the first image; a character or style sheet works well.\n- **Timeline**: drag the yellow handles to set the range, double-click a shot to split it, right-click a cut to merge, *One shot* for a single long shot. Hover it for hints, **?** lists every control, **Analyse** shows the exact cuts without rendering.\n\n**This version: hits that land.** Full model, 30 steps, CFG 5 with the negative zeroed before the guide, so the picture is pushed onto the audio.\n\nNodes: Syntax Timeline and the optional Syntax Preview Strip (the sync bar along the bottom; delete it to hide); everything else is core."
   ]
  },
